# (build 142) Rolf's picture only where his art is loaded. His two windows
# draw tiles $4A0 on, where BuildingScreen puts RolfPortraitArt with his
# palette on line 1 -- in every building but the library (the graph, with
# its own palette, is at those tiles: LibrGraphPortArt), the roof, Tyler's
# spaceship and the Esper mansion. A binding by window or by tile range
# alone would draw Rolf's picture over whatever those tiles hold there.
#
# The game never opens Rolf's window in the library; this route does, by
# naming portrait 0 at the library's door, so the window draws the graph's
# tiles through Rolf's map -- as the ROM would -- and the pixel is the
# tiles', not his picture's. With the picture bound regardless of what is
# loaded, `expect picture` says rolf and colour_check finds about a
# thousand pixels a frame in Rolf's grey where the graph's blue is (build
# 142 checked it so).
# Fails on b141d: the probe has no `expect picture`.
#
# (build 146a) No portrait art goes to VRAM now, the graph's at $4A0 no
# more than Rolf's: the window's inside is empty -- black -- where it drew
# the graph's tiles through Rolf's map. The gate still holds (no Rolf
# picture where his art would not be); the frames are the one route whose
# colours 146a changed.

start building 10 0 0 0 32 16       # the library, portrait 0: Rolf's window
wait idle
expect picture 40 40 none           # inside Rolf's window: no picture
expect picture 258 70 none
shot 01_rolf_window_in_library
